From: SF2000 Linux <sf2000@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] qpsx: keep dynamic memory fast on NOMMU

The SF2000 Linux target is NOMMU and deliberately builds QPSX without
SHMEM_MIRRORING or TMPFS_MIRRORING.  In that configuration psxM is allocated
by malloc and the recompiler must use the checked psxMemRead/Write helpers.

The upstream source also enables constant-address emission unconditionally.
That optimization converts a PSX address to a host pointer while compiling a
block, so make it an explicit platform contract: it is valid only while psxM
has a stable lifetime. Dynamic accesses retain their runtime range check and
psxM conversion. Keeping both paths behind build options prevents a future
allocation or mapping change from silently altering generated code.

The previous version of this patch replaced the upstream non-mapped address
range check with a 0x1f800000 mask.  That changed the original bit-27 RAM
classification and caused Ridge Racer to stop producing frames after startup
in QEMU.  Keep the upstream range check unchanged; it is the known-good
predicate for this recompiler path.

--- a/src/recompiler/mips/recompiler.cpp
+++ b/src/recompiler/mips/recompiler.cpp
@@ -79,1 +79,3 @@
-#define USE_CONST_ADDRESSES
+#if defined(QPSX_ENABLE_MIPS_CONST_MEM) && QPSX_ENABLE_MIPS_CONST_MEM
+#define USE_CONST_ADDRESSES
+#endif
@@ -82,1 +84,3 @@
-#define USE_CONST_FUZZY_ADDRESSES
+#if defined(QPSX_ENABLE_MIPS_CONST_MEM) && QPSX_ENABLE_MIPS_CONST_MEM
+#define USE_CONST_FUZZY_ADDRESSES
+#endif
@@ -84,2 +88,11 @@
-/* Generate inline memory access or call psxMemRead/Write C functions */
-#define USE_DIRECT_MEM_ACCESS
+/*
+ * Generate inline memory access or call psxMemRead/Write C functions.
+ *
+ * Dynamic accesses perform a runtime PSX-range check and convert through the
+ * malloc-backed psxM pointer when no virtual mapping is available.  Keep this
+ * fast path explicit because constant-address emission has the separate,
+ * stricter requirement that psxM remain allocated at one address.
+ */
+#if defined(QPSX_ENABLE_MIPS_DIRECT_MEM) && QPSX_ENABLE_MIPS_DIRECT_MEM
+#define USE_DIRECT_MEM_ACCESS
+#endif

--- a/src/recompiler/mips/mips_codegen.h
+++ b/src/recompiler/mips/mips_codegen.h
@@ -352,1 +352,2 @@
-    write32(0x0c000000 | (((u32)(addr) & 0x0fffffff) >> 2));                   \
+    LI32(MIPSREG_T9, (u32)(addr));                                              \
+    write32(0x0000f809 | (MIPSREG_T9 << 21));                                  \
--- a/src/recompiler/mips/rec_lsu.cpp.h
+++ b/src/recompiler/mips/rec_lsu.cpp.h
@@ -75,2 +75,4 @@
 /* Cache values in host regs in load/store emitters. */
-#define USE_LSU_CACHING
+#if defined(QPSX_ENABLE_MIPS_LSU_CACHING) && QPSX_ENABLE_MIPS_LSU_CACHING
+#define USE_LSU_CACHING
+#endif
